# The committed fixutf8 bytecode is PEP 552 checked-hash, keyed to a hash of
# these files' exact bytes. Git for Windows offers core.autocrlf=true as its
# installer default, which would check them out CRLF and so invalidate every
# committed .pyc: the checker reports all three as compiled from something
# else, and regenerating there keys the bytecode to CRLF and fails CI instead.
MercurialExtensions/fixutf8/*.py text eol=lf